      "title": "Trump attacks ‘migrants and communists’ as he tries to exploit France unrest",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/trump-france-protests",
      "description": "<p>President at Kansas rally tries to turn protests into cautionary tale for US as Republicans face midterm losses</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/europe-protests-france-spain-portugal-2026-explainer\">Explainer: why are people protesting across Europe?</a></p></li></ul><p>As Republicans confront mounting political headwinds ahead of November’s midterm elections, Donald Trump is attempting to turn unrest in France into a cautionary tale for American voters, recasting the demonstrations that began as student protests against crumbling schools and the soaring <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/19/the-guardian-view-on-frances-protests-a-polarised-country-is-in-a-perilous-political-moment\">cost of living</a> as evidence of the dangers of immigration and the erosion of western civilization.</p><p>At a rally in Kansas on Monday evening, Trump described France as a once-great nation that had been “conquered, looted, and burned to the ground by migrants, jihadists, and communists”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/trump-france-protests\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T02:01:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "French authorities announce partial curfews as PM blames ‘ultra-left’ for exploiting protests – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/19/europe-france-protests-riots-macron-ukraine-russia-zelenskyy-sweden-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This live blog is now closed.</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/french-government-crisis-talks-violent-unrest-policing-macron\">Macron criticises ‘unbridled violence’ after 2,400 arrests across France</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>French PM Lecornu says he has asked prefects to implement “a number of partial curfews” in certain “localised” urban areas to stop further disorder, </strong>which he attributes to “the extreme-left” and some criminal elements.</p><p><strong>We will no doubt hear more on this from local authorities,</strong> as in the example of Marseille (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/19/europe-france-protests-riots-macron-ukraine-russia-zelenskyy-sweden-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ad5d5088f0862b813bc4c4a#block-6ad5d5088f0862b813bc4c4a\">10:32</a>).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/19/europe-france-protests-riots-macron-ukraine-russia-zelenskyy-sweden-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
